      "findings": [
        {
          "dimension": "feasibility and trick counting",
          "fact": "The club route is feasible and the conditional trick counts are correct.",
          "explanation": "South holds CA CK C8 C6 C4 opposite CQ C7 C2. Cashing CA, crossing to CQ and returning toward CK produces five club tricks on 3–2, or four after conceding one on 4–1. SA, HA, HK, DA and DK supply five outside winners. D3 legally follows the diamond lead.",
          "quotes": [
            "Cash the club ace, lead a low club to dummy's queen, then return a club toward the king, adjusting to revealed distribution.",
            "A 3–2 break gives ten tricks; against 4–1, concede a club to establish the ninth trick."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
